# draco-deployment.skill - Phase 12: Continuous Learning & Self-Optimizing

## Purpose
Phase 12 skill for continuous learning, heuristic refinement, and self-optimizing system deployment. Enables auto-improvement through feedback loops, heuristic refinement, and profile auto-updating.

## Core Features

### Continuous Learning
- **Learning Enabled**: True (default)
- **Auto-Update Frequency**: 24h (default)
- **Heuristic Refinement**: CMA-ES algorithm (50 heuristics per cycle)
- **Expected Improvement**: 0.3 (default)
- **A/B Testing**: Enabled (minimum 100 samples)
- **Degradation Threshold**: 0.85 (85% quality retention)
- **Self-Healing Strategies**: revert, adjust, retrain, update

### Profile Auto-Update
- **Scheduler**: 24h default frequency
- **Versioning**: Semantic versioning (v1.0, v1.1, etc.)
- **Rollback Support**: Enabled (auto-revert on degradation)
- **Update Triggers**: quality drop >15%, user corrections, scheduled

### Feedback Collection
- **Source Types**: user corrections, performance metrics, agent feedback, quality gates
- **Collection Rate**: per-operation default
- **Storage**: JSON-based history with timestamps
- **Retention**: 90 days default

### A/B Testing Framework
- **Minimum Samples**: 100
- **Confidence Level**: 95% default
- **Test Duration**: minimum 24h
- **Success Criteria**: improvement > expected_improvement (0.3 default)

### Degradation Detection
- **Monitoring**: continuous quality score tracking
- **Threshold**: quality drop >15% from baseline
- **Actions**: trigger self-healing, alert administrators, log event
- **Recovery**: automatic revert or adjust strategies

### Self-Optimization Loop
1. Collect feedback from recent operations
2. Run CMA-ES heuristic refinement (50 heuristics)
3. Evaluate A/B test results
4. Update profiles and configuration
5. Deploy improvements if quality threshold maintained
6. Log results for trend analysis
7. Repeat cycle

## Deployment Configuration

### System Settings
- `continuous_learning`: True (enabled default)
- `auto_update`: True (24h frequency)
- `heuristic_refinement`: CMA-ES (50 heuristics per cycle)
- `ab_testing`: True (minimum 100 samples)
- `degradation_detection`: True (threshold: 0.85)
- `self_healing`: True (4 strategies: revert, adjust, retrain, update)

### Update Triggers
- Quality score drops below 85% of baseline
- User provides explicit correction
- Scheduled update (every 24h)
- New agent integration
- Configuration change

### Rollback Protocol
1. Detect degradation via quality monitoring
2. Auto-revert to previous configuration
3. Log degradation event with timestamp
4. Notify administrators (if enabled)
5. Resume normal operation with previous settings

## Integration Points

### With Phase 11 (Testing & Validation)
- Quality gate results feed into degradation detection
- Test outcomes inform heuristic refinement
- A/B test results validate optimization strategies

### With Phase 10 (Agent Integration)
- Agent-specific quality thresholds update via YAGNI ladder
- Agent profile auto-updates based on performance
- Reduction cap adjustments per agent type

### With Phase 9 (Quantization/Pruning)
- Pruning sparsity targets auto-tune based on quality metrics
- Quantization bit allocation optimizes for current workload
- Model-aware adjustments per LLM type

### With Phase 8 (ZON Format)
- Compression depth auto-adjusts based on quality preservation
- Readability modes optimize for current agent profiles
- Schema versioning stays current with best practices

### With Phase 7 (Verdict-First)
- Verdict accuracy improves with continuous learning
- Compression ratio optimization feeds into verdict selection
- Technical tag generation updates with new patterns

### With Phase 6 (Noise Cancellation)
- Verbose phrase patterns update based on user feedback
- Importance scoring refinements from correction data
- Classification model updates from new labeled data

### With Phase 5 (YAML Filters)
- Filter rules auto-optimize based on effectiveness data
- Importance/frequency thresholds adjust to current content
- Rule conflict resolution updates from violation logs

### With Phase 4 (Hybrid RAG)
- BM25 + ONNX weights adjust based on search quality
- Relevance scoring improves with feedback loop
- Multi-vector search parameters update

### With Phase 3 (Tree-sitter)
- Codebase skeleton updates reflect optimization changes
- Import graph refinements from agent usage patterns
- Build/test pattern updates from deployment data

### With Phase 2 (MCP Protocol)
- Zero-LLM routing confidence thresholds update
- Deterministic command patterns refine from usage
- Transport protocol preferences update

### With Phase 1 (Baseline & Metrics)
- Baseline measurements refresh with new data
- Token profiling updates from continuous analysis
- Metric set adjustments based on quality trends

## Quality Gates (Phase 11 Integration)

### 200+ Quality Gates Monitored
- Reduction gate: ensures 90%+ token reduction target
- Quality gate: ensures 90%+ quality preservation
- Agent gate: validates per-agent reduction caps
- ZON gate: verifies lossless compression integrity
- Quantization gate: checks sparsity/quality balance
- MCP gate: validates zero-LLM routing decisions
- Agent gate: checks YAGNI level compliance
- Format gate: ensures ZON schema compliance
- Noise gate: validates noise reduction percentages
- Verdict gate: checks verdict-first output accuracy

### Depletion Detection Triggers
- Quality score drop >15% from baseline
- Reduction rate below 85% of target
- Agent compatibility degradation
- Self-healing failure events
- A/B test inconclusiveness

### Self-Healing Actions
- **revert**: restore previous configuration
- **adjust**: fine-tune parameters within safe bounds
- **retrain**: update models with new data
- **update**: deploy improved configuration

